   "fen": "r2q1rk1/pp2ppbp/3pbnp1/8/2P1P3/2N1B3/PP1QBPPP/R4RK1 b - - 7 11",
   "line": [
    "Be6",
    "O-O"
   ],
   "spoken": "You play a bishop to e6, developing; White usually castles.",
   "reanchor": true
  },
  {
   "ply": 22,
   "t": 3330.5,
   "fen": "r4rk1/pp2ppbp/3pbnp1/q7/2P1P3/2N1B3/PP1QBPPP/R4RK1 w - - 8 12",
   "line": [
    "Qa5"
   ],
   "spoken": "The main move is a queen to a5, piling pressure on White's queenside — very hard to play for White without deep theory.",
   "reanchor": true
  },
  {
   "ply": 23,
   "t": 3345.5,
   "fen": "r4rk1/pp2ppbp/3pbnp1/q2N4/2P1P3/4B3/PP1QBPPP/R4RK1 b - - 9 12",
   "line": [
    "Nd5"
   ],
   "spoken": "A lot of people are tempted by a knight to d5, a common tactic...",
   "reanchor": true
  },
  {
   "ply": 24,
   "t": 3350.5,
   "fen": "r4rk1/pp2ppbp/3pbnp1/3N4/2P1P3/4B3/PP1qBPPP/R4RK1 w - - 0 13",
   "line": [
    "Qxd2"
   ],
   "spoken": "...but it doesn't work here, because after the trade on d2 White has an intermezzo capture on e7.",
   "reanchor": true
  },
  {
   "ply": 25,
   "t": 3352,
   "fen": "r4rk1/pp2Npbp/3pbnp1/8/2P1P3/4B3/PP1qBPPP/R4RK1 b - - 0 13",
   "line": [
    "Nxe7+"
   ],
   "spoken": ""
  },
  {
   "ply": 27,
   "t": 3354.5,
   "fen": "r4r1k/pp2Npbp/3pbnp1/8/2P1P3/8/PP1BBPPP/R4RK1 b - - 0 14",
   "line": [
    "Kh8",
    "Bxd2"
   ],
   "spoken": "The line doesn't end there — Black plays a knight capture on c4 with a huge initiative, White's knight stranded, everything hanging — better for Black.",
   "reanchor": true
  },
  {
   "ply": 28,
   "t": 3356,
   "fen": "r4r1k/pp2Npbp/3pb1p1/8/2P1n3/8/PP1BBPPP/R4RK1 w - - 0 15",
   "line": [
    "Nxe4"
   ],
   "spoken": ""
  },
  {
   "ply": 22,
   "t": 3363,
   "fen": "r4rk1/pp2ppbp/3pbnp1/q7/2P1P3/2N1B3/PP1QBPPP/R4RK1 w - - 8 12",
   "line": [],
   "spoken": ""
  },
  {
   "ply": 23,
   "t": 3365,
   "fen": "r4rk1/pp2ppbp/3pbnp1/q7/2P1P3/1PN1B3/P2QBPPP/R4RK1 b - - 0 12",
   "line": [
    "b3"
   ],
   "spoken": "If White plays b3 to reinforce c4, that's a good move.",
   "reanchor": true
  },
  {
   "ply": 24,
   "t": 3376.5,
   "fen": "r1r3k1/pp2ppbp/3pbnp1/q7/2P1P3/1PN1B3/P2QBPPP/R4RK1 w - - 1 13",
   "line": [
    "Rfc8"
   ],
   "spoken": "Black's best is a rook to c8.",
   "reanchor": true
  },
  {
   "ply": 25,
   "t": 3379.5,
   "fen": "r1r3k1/pp2ppbp/3pbnp1/q7/2P1P3/1PN1BP2/P2QB1PP/R4RK1 b - - 0 13",
   "line": [
    "f3"
   ],
   "spoken": "If White sleepwalks with f3...",
   "reanchor": true
  },
  {
   "ply": 26,
   "t": 3386.5,
   "fen": "r1r3k1/1p2ppbp/p2pbnp1/q7/2P1P3/1PN1BP2/P2QB1PP/R4RK1 w - - 0 14",
   "line": [
    "a6"
   ],
   "spoken": "...Black develops a huge initiative with a6, preparing b5, which is dangerous because White can't capture — the c3 knight hangs.",
   "reanchor": true
  },
  {
   "ply": 27,
   "t": 3397.5,
   "fen": "r1r3k1/1p2ppbp/p2pbnp1/q7/2P1P3/1PN1BP2/P2QB1PP/2R2RK1 b - - 1 14",
   "line": [
    "Rac1"
   ],
   "spoken": "If White defends the knight with a rook to c1...",
   "reanchor": true
  },
  {
   "ply": 28,
   "t": 3400,
   "fen": "r1r3k1/4ppbp/p2pbnp1/qp6/2P1P3/1PN1BP2/P2QB1PP/2R2RK1 w - - 0 15",
   "line": [
    "b5"
   ],
   "spoken": "...Black still plays b5, because after the captures...",
   "reanchor": true
  },
  {
   "ply": 29,
   "t": 3403.5,
   "fen": "r1r3k1/4ppbp/p2pbnp1/qP6/4P3/1PN1BP2/P2QB1PP/2R2RK1 b - - 0 15",
   "line": [
    "cxb5"
   ],
   "spoken": ""
  },
  {
   "ply": 30,
   "t": 3404.5,
   "fen": "r1r3k1/4ppbp/3pbnp1/qp6/4P3/1PN1BP2/P2QB1PP/2R2RK1 w - - 0 16",
   "line": [
    "axb5"
   ],
   "spoken": "...White collapses on the queenside.",
   "reanchor": true
  },
  {
   "ply": 31,
   "t": 3408,
   "fen": "r1r3k1/4ppbp/3pbnp1/qB6/4P3/1PN1BP2/P2Q2PP/2R2RK1 b - - 0 16",
   "line": [
    "Bxb5"
   ],
   "spoken": "If a bishop takes on b5, what's the simple powerful move that makes it work?",
   "reanchor": true
  },
  {
   "ply": 32,
   "t": 3419,
   "fen": "r5k1/4ppbp/3pbnp1/qB6/4P3/1Pr1BP2/P2Q2PP/2R2RK1 w - - 0 17",
   "line": [
    "Rxc3"
   ],
   "spoken": "This is why the rook went to c8 — a rook capture on c3.",
   "reanchor": true
  },
  {
   "ply": 34,
   "t": 3422.5,
   "fen": "r5k1/4ppbp/3pbnp1/1q6/4P3/1PQ1BP2/P5PP/2R2RK1 w - - 0 18",
   "line": [
    "Qxc3",
    "Qxb5"
   ],
   "spoken": "Two pieces for a rook usually benefits the minor pieces, especially in a middlegame with an open center.",
   "reanchor": true
  },
  {
   "ply": 32,
   "t": 3429,
   "fen": "r5k1/4ppbp/3pbnp1/qB6/4P3/1Pr1BP2/P2Q2PP/2R2RK1 w - - 0 17",
   "line": [],
   "spoken": ""
  },
  {
   "ply": 33,
   "t": 3430,
   "fen": "r5k1/4ppbp/3pbnp1/qB6/4P3/1PR1BP2/P2Q2PP/5RK1 b - - 0 17",
   "line": [
    "Rxc3"
   ],
   "spoken": ""
  },
  {
   "ply": 34,
   "t": 3431.5,
   "fen": "r5k1/4ppbp/3pb1p1/qB6/4n3/1PR1BP2/P2Q2PP/5RK1 w - - 0 18",
   "line": [
    "Nxe4"
   ],
   "spoken": "After the rook capture there's also a knight capture on e4, even sexier — you recapture the rook and everything hangs.",
   "reanchor": true
  },
  {
   "ply": 30,
   "t": 3440,
   "fen": "r1r3k1/4ppbp/3pbnp1/qp6/4P3/1PN1BP2/P2QB1PP/2R2RK1 w - - 0 16",
   "line": [],
   "spoken": ""
  },
  {
   "ply": 31,
   "t": 3441.5,
   "fen": "r1r3k1/4ppbp/3pbnp1/qN6/4P3/1P2BP2/P2QB1PP/2R2RK1 b - - 0 16",
   "line": [
    "Nxb5"
   ],
   "spoken": ""
  },
  {
   "ply": 32,
   "t": 3444,
   "fen": "r1r3k1/4ppbp/3pbnp1/1N6/4P3/1P2BP2/P2qB1PP/2R2RK1 w - - 0 17",
   "line": [
    "Qxd2"
   ],
   "spoken": "If White plays a knight capture on b5, we take the queen.",
   "reanchor": true
  },
  {
   "ply": 33,
   "t": 3447.5,
   "fen": "r1R3k1/4ppbp/3pbnp1/1N6/4P3/1P2BP2/P2qB1PP/5RK1 b - - 0 17",
   "line": [
    "Rxc8+"
   ],
   "spoken": ""
  },
  {
   "ply": 34,
   "t": 3450.5,
   "fen": "r1b3k1/4ppbp/3p1np1/1N6/4P3/1P2BP2/P2qB1PP/5RK1 w - - 0 18",
   "line": [
    "Bxc8"
   ],
   "spoken": "After a rook check we recapture and take on a2...",
   "reanchor": true
  },
  {
   "ply": 35,
   "t": 3452,
   "fen": "r1b3k1/4ppbp/3p1np1/1N6/4P3/1P3P2/P2BB1PP/5RK1 b - - 0 18",
   "line": [
    "Bxd2"
   ],
   "spoken": ""
  },
  {
   "ply": 36,
   "t": 3453.5,
   "fen": "2b3k1/4ppbp/3p1np1/1N6/4P3/1P3P2/r2BB1PP/5RK1 w - - 0 19",
   "line": [
    "Rxa2"
   ],
   "spoken": "...with a huge initiative into the endgame.",
   "reanchor": true
  },
  {
   "ply": 37,
   "t": 3455.5,
   "fen": "2b3k1/4ppbp/3p1np1/1N6/4P3/1P3P2/r2BB1PP/3R2K1 b - - 1 19",
   "line": [
    "Rd1"
   ],
   "spoken": "After a rook to d1 we redeploy the bishop to e6...",
   "reanchor": true
  },
  {
   "ply": 38,
   "t": 3456.5,
   "fen": "6k1/4ppbp/3pbnp1/1N6/4P3/1P3P2/r2BB1PP/3R2K1 w - - 2 20",
   "line": [
    "Be6"
   ],
   "spoken": "...and start tickling that pawn — White is getting tortured.",
   "reanchor": true
  },
  {
   "ply": 26,
   "t": 3463,
   "fen": "r1r3k1/1p2ppbp/p2pbnp1/q7/2P1P3/1PN1BP2/P2QB1PP/R4RK1 w - - 0 14",
   "line": [],
   "spoken": ""
  },
  {
   "ply": 27,
   "t": 3466,
   "fen": "r1r3k1/1p2ppbp/p2pbnp1/q7/P1P1P3/1PN1BP2/3QB1PP/R4RK1 b - - 0 14",
   "line": [
    "a4"
   ],
   "spoken": "White can play a4 to stop b5.",
   "reanchor": true
  },
  {
   "ply": 29,
   "t": 3471.5,
   "fen": "r1r3k1/4ppbp/p2pbnp1/qP6/2P1P3/1PN1BP2/3QB1PP/R4RK1 b - - 0 15",
   "line": [
    "b5",
    "axb5"
   ],
   "spoken": "Now you shouldn't play b5, because of a discovered attack on the queen.",
   "reanchor": true
  },
  {
   "ply": 27,
   "t": 3474,
   "fen": "r1r3k1/1p2ppbp/p2pbnp1/q7/P1P1P3/1PN1BP2/3QB1PP/R4RK1 b - - 0 14",
   "line": [],
   "spoken": "But whenever a4 is played in the Accelerated Dragon, the b3 pawn becomes a permanent weakness.",
   "reanchor": true
  },
  {
   "ply": 28,
   "t": 3483.5,
   "fen": "r1r3k1/1p2ppbp/p2pbnp1/8/PqP1P3/1PN1BP2/3QB1PP/R4RK1 w - - 1 15",
   "line": [
    "Qb4"
   ],
   "spoken": "One tool is to plant the queen on that weak square.",
   "reanchor": true
  },
  {
   "ply": 29,
   "t": 3486.5,
   "fen": "r1r3k1/1p2ppbp/p2pbnp1/8/PqP1P3/1PN1BP2/3QB1PP/1R3RK1 b - - 2 15",
   "line": [
    "Rab1"
   ],
   "spoken": "White is forced to defend the pawn.",
   "reanchor": true
  },
  {
   "ply": 30,
   "t": 3490,
   "fen": "r1r3k1/1p1nppbp/p2pb1p1/8/PqP1P3/1PN1BP2/3QB1PP/1R3RK1 w - - 3 16",
   "line": [
    "Nd7"
   ],
   "spoken": "Then remember the maneuver, a knight from f6 to d7 — strong, opening an attack on the c-file and eyeing c5.",
   "reanchor": true
  },
  {
   "ply": 31,
   "t": 3499.5,
   "fen": "r1r3k1/1p1nppbp/p2pb1p1/8/PqP1P3/1PN1BP2/3QB1PP/1RR3K1 b - - 4 16",
   "line": [
    "Rfc1"
   ],
   "spoken": ""
  },
  {
   "ply": 32,
   "t": 3501.5,
   "fen": "r1r3k1/3nppbp/p2pb1p1/1p6/PqP1P3/1PN1BP2/3QB1PP/1RR3K1 w - - 0 17",
   "line": [
    "b5"
   ],
   "spoken": "After a rook to c1 we play b5.",
   "reanchor": true
  },
  {
   "ply": 34,
   "t": 3505,
   "fen": "r1r3k1/3nppbp/3pb1p1/1p6/1qP1P3/1PN1BP2/3QB1PP/1RR3K1 w - - 0 18",
   "line": [
    "axb5",
    "axb5"
   ],
   "spoken": "And if a capture on b5, we win the knight.",
   "reanchor": true
  },
  {
   "ply": 36,
   "t": 3509.5,
   "fen": "r1r3k1/3npp1p/3pb1p1/1P6/1q2P3/1Pb1BP2/3QB1PP/1RR3K1 w - - 0 19",
   "line": [
    "cxb5",
    "Bxc3"
   ],
   "spoken": ""
  },
  {
   "ply": 34,
   "t": 3510.5,
   "fen": "r1r3k1/3nppbp/3pb1p1/1p6/1qP1P3/1PN1BP2/3QB1PP/1RR3K1 w - - 0 18",
   "line": [],
   "spoken": ""
  },
  {
   "ply": 35,
   "t": 3511.5,
   "fen": "r1r3k1/3nppbp/3pb1p1/1N6/1qP1P3/1P2BP2/3QB1PP/1RR3K1 b - - 0 18",
   "line": [
    "Nxb5"
   ],
   "spoken": "If a knight captures on b5, what's the correct sequence?",
   "reanchor": true
  },
  {
   "ply": 36,
   "t": 3528.5,
   "fen": "r1r3k1/3nppbp/3pb1p1/1N6/2P1P3/1P2BP2/3qB1PP/1RR3K1 w - - 0 19",
   "line": [
    "Qxd2"
   ],
   "spoken": ""
  },
  {
   "ply": 37,
   "t": 3530.5,
   "fen": "r1r3k1/3nppbp/3pb1p1/1N6/2P1P3/1P3P2/3BB1PP/1RR3K1 b - - 0 19",
   "line": [
    "Bxd2"
   ],
   "spoken": "The key: when you sac a pawn, don't rule out a queen trade — it doesn't diminish anything, and here it skewers the bishops.",
   "reanchor": true
  },
  {
   "ply": 38,
   "t": 3533.5,
   "fen": "2r3k1/3nppbp/3pb1p1/1N6/2P1P3/1P3P2/r2BB1PP/1RR3K1 w - - 1 20",
   "line": [
    "Ra2"
   ],
   "spoken": ""
  },
  {
   "ply": 39,
   "t": 3536.5,
   "fen": "2r3k1/3nppbp/3pb1p1/1N6/2P1P3/1P3P2/r2BB1PP/1R1R2K1 b - - 2 20",
   "line": [
    "Rd1"
   ],
   "spoken": "After a rook to d1 it's time to start a fire on the other side of the board.",
   "reanchor": true
  },
  {
   "ply": 40,
   "t": 3560.5,
   "fen": "2r3k1/3np1bp/3pb1p1/1N3p2/2P1P3/1P3P2/r2BB1PP/1R1R2K1 w - - 0 21",
   "line": [
    "f5"
   ],
   "spoken": "To translate our edge into an advantage we keep creating threats — a very timely f5, a typical Accelerated Dragon idea.",
   "reanchor": true
  },
  {
   "ply": 41,
   "t": 3565.5,
   "fen": "2r3k1/3np1bp/3pb1p1/1N3P2/2P5/1P3P2/r2BB1PP/1R1R2K1 b - - 0 21",
   "line": [
    "exf5"
   ],
   "spoken": "If White captures on f5, you play a bishop recapture...",
   "reanchor": true
  },
  {
   "ply": 42,
   "t": 3566.5,
   "fen": "2r3k1/3np1bp/3p2p1/1N3b2/2P5/1P3P2/r2BB1PP/1R1R2K1 w - - 0 22",
   "line": [
    "Bxf5"
   ],
   "spoken": ""
  },
  {
   "ply": 43,
   "t": 3567.5,
   "fen": "2r3k1/3np1bp/3p2p1/1N3b2/2P5/1P3P2/r2BB1PP/2RR2K1 b - - 1 22",
   "line": [
    "Rbc1"
   ],
   "spoken": "...then, after a rook to c1, either a bishop to b2 trapping the rook or a knight to c5 — White has no good defense.",
   "reanchor": true
  },
  {
   "ply": 44,
   "t": 3571.5,
   "fen": "2r3k1/4p1bp/3p2p1/1Nn2b2/2P5/1P3P2/r2BB1PP/2RR2K1 w - - 2 23",
   "line": [
    "Nc5"
   ],
   "spoken": "Just look at the extent of Black's domination.",
   "reanchor": true
  },
  {
   "ply": 40,
   "t": 3578.5,
   "fen": "2r3k1/3np1bp/3pb1p1/1N3p2/2P1P3/1P3P2/r2BB1PP/1R1R2K1 w - - 0 21",
   "line": [],
   "spoken": "What if White ignores it? It's not easy to move — White is so paralyzed.",
   "reanchor": true
  },
  {
   "ply": 41,
   "t": 3585,
   "fen": "2r3k1/3np1bp/3pb1p1/1N3p2/2P1P3/1P3P1P/r2BB1P1/1R1R2K1 b - - 0 21",
   "line": [
    "h3"
   ],
   "spoken": "Say White plays h3...",
   "reanchor": true
  },
  {
   "ply": 42,
   "t": 3588.5,
   "fen": "2r3k1/4p1bp/3pb1p1/1Nn2p2/2P1P3/1P3P1P/r2BB1P1/1R1R2K1 w - - 1 22",
   "line": [
    "Nc5"
   ],
   "spoken": "...we play a knight to c5, already attacking e4, and White starts to collapse.",
   "reanchor": true
  },
  {
   "ply": 43,
   "t": 3593.5,
   "fen": "2r3k1/4p1bp/3pb1p1/1Nn2p2/1PP1P3/5P1P/r2BB1P1/1R1R2K1 b - - 0 22",
   "line": [
    "b4"
   ],
   "spoken": "White can play b4 to chase the knight...",
   "reanchor": true
  },
  {
   "ply": 44,
   "t": 3595.5,
   "fen": "2r3k1/4p1bp/3pb1p1/1N3p2/nPP1P3/5P1P/r2BB1P1/1R1R2K1 w - - 1 23",
   "line": [
    "Na4"
   ],
   "spoken": "...but it squeezes into a4, c4 is weak, and White can't move the rook because the bishop hangs.",
   "reanchor": true
  },
  {
   "ply": 35,
   "t": 3606.5,
   "fen": "r1r3k1/3nppbp/3pb1p1/1N6/1qP1P3/1P2BP2/3QB1PP/1RR3K1 b - - 0 18",
   "line": [],
   "spoken": "Like the Grünfeld, the Accelerated is about the power of piece activity and the willingness to sacrifice.",
   "reanchor": true
  },
  {
   "ply": 31,
   "t": 3609,
   "fen": "r1r3k1/1p1nppbp/p2pb1p1/8/PqP1P3/1PN1BP2/3QB1PP/1RR3K1 b - - 4 16",
   "line": [],
   "spoken": "When you sacrifice, you don't have to win in two or three moves — you can play for a long time.",
   "reanchor": true
  },
  {
   "ply": 30,
   "t": 3632,
   "fen": "r1r3k1/1p1nppbp/p2pb1p1/8/PqP1P3/1PN1BP2/3QB1PP/1R3RK1 w - - 3 16",
   "line": [],
   "spoken": "Down a pawn or even a piece, as long as your pieces are active — the concept of squeezing and applying pressure.",
   "reanchor": true
  },
  {
   "ply": 29,
   "t": 3633.5,
   "fen": "r1r3k1/1p2ppbp/p2pbnp1/8/PqP1P3/1PN1BP2/3QB1PP/1R3RK1 b - - 2 15",
   "line": [],
   "spoken": ""
  },
  {
   "ply": 22,
   "t": 3637,
   "fen": "r4rk1/pp2ppbp/3pbnp1/q7/2P1P3/2N1B3/PP1QBPPP/R4RK1 w - - 8 12",
   "line": [],
   "spoken": ""
  },
  {
   "ply": 16,
   "t": 3640,
   "fen": "r1bqk2r/pp2ppbp/3p1np1/8/2PQP3/2N5/PP2BPPP/R1B1K2R w KQkq - 2 9",
   "line": [],
   "spoken": ""
  },
  {
   "ply": 18,
   "t": 3642,
   "fen": "r1bqkb1r/pp2pp1p/3p1np1/8/2PQP3/2N5/PP3PPP/R1B1KB1R w KQkq - 4 10",
   "line": [
    "Bf1",
    "Bf8"
   ],
   "spoken": "The main line against a bishop to g7 is a bishop to e3.",
   "reanchor": true
  },
  {
   "ply": 19,
   "t": 3654,
   "fen": "r1bqkb1r/pp2pp1p/3p1np1/8/2PQP3/2N5/PP2BPPP/R1B1K2R b KQkq - 5 10",
   "line": [
    "Be2"
   ],
   "spoken": "The line once considered best is a bishop to g5.",
   "reanchor": true
  },
  {
   "ply": 21,
   "t": 3656,
   "fen": "r1bqk2r/pp2ppbp/3p1np1/6B1/2PQP3/2N5/PP2BPPP/R3K2R b KQkq - 7 11",
   "line": [
    "Bg7",
    "Bg5"
   ],
   "spoken": ""
  },
  {
   "ply": 23,
   "t": 3661.5,
   "fen": "r1bq1rk1/pp2ppbp/3p1np1/6B1/2PQP3/2N5/PP2BPPP/R4RK1 b - - 9 12",
   "line": [
    "O-O",
    "O-O"
   ],
   "spoken": "Here Black has no good discovery, because that bishop is invulnerable...",
   "reanchor": true
  },
  {
   "ply": 24,
   "t": 3669.5,
   "fen": "r2q1rk1/pp2ppbp/3pbnp1/6B1/2PQP3/2N5/PP2BPPP/R4RK1 w - - 10 13",
   "line": [
    "Be6"
   ],
   "spoken": "...but our strategy barely changes — we still play a bishop to e6, still threatening a knight to d5.",
   "reanchor": true
  },
  {
   "ply": 25,
   "t": 3672.5,
   "fen": "r2q1rk1/pp2ppbp/3pbnp1/6B1/2P1P3/2N5/PP1QBPPP/R4RK1 b - - 11 13",
   "line": [
    "Qd2"
   ],
   "spoken": "So White is forced back to d2, and we play a queen to a5 — the same moves against everything.",
   "reanchor": true
  },
  {
   "ply": 26,
   "t": 3678.5,
   "fen": "r4rk1/pp2ppbp/3pbnp1/q5B1/2P1P3/2N5/PP1QBPPP/R4RK1 w - - 12 14",
   "line": [
    "Qa5"
   ],
   "spoken": ""
  },
  {
   "ply": 27,
   "t": 3683,
   "fen": "r4rk1/pp2ppbp/3pbnpB/q7/2P1P3/2N5/PP1QBPPP/R4RK1 b - - 13 14",
   "line": [
    "Bh6"
   ],
   "spoken": "Very often White plays a bishop to h6 in these positions — a bad move.",
   "reanchor": true
  },
  {
   "ply": 29,
   "t": 3692,
   "fen": "r4rk1/pp2pp1p/3pbnpQ/q7/2P1P3/2N5/PP2BPPP/R4RK1 b - - 0 15",
   "line": [
    "Bxh6",
    "Qxh6"
   ],
   "spoken": "You give up your fianchettoed bishop, but look how weak White's pawns become — the simplest way to pick them off...",
   "reanchor": true
  },
  {
   "ply": 30,
   "t": 3695.5,
   "fen": "2r2rk1/pp2pp1p/3pbnpQ/q7/2P1P3/2N5/PP2BPPP/R4RK1 w - - 1 16",
   "line": [
    "Rac8"
   ],
   "spoken": "...is a rook to c8.",
   "reanchor": true
  },
  {
   "ply": 31,
   "t": 3699,
   "fen": "2r2rk1/pp2pp1p/3pbnpQ/q7/2P1P3/1PN5/P3BPPP/R4RK1 b - - 0 16",
   "line": [
    "b3"
   ],
   "spoken": "White can't play b3 — a common blunder.",
   "reanchor": true
  },
  {
   "ply": 32,
   "t": 3701,
   "fen": "2r2rk1/pp2pp1p/3pbnpQ/8/2P1P3/1Pq5/P3BPPP/R4RK1 w - - 0 17",
   "line": [
    "Qxc3"
   ],
   "spoken": "It drops to a capture on c3.",
   "reanchor": true
  },
  {
   "ply": 30,
   "t": 3703,
   "fen": "2r2rk1/pp2pp1p/3pbnpQ/q7/2P1P3/2N5/PP2BPPP/R4RK1 w - - 1 16",
   "line": [],
   "spoken": ""
  },
  {
   "ply": 31,
   "t": 3705,
   "fen": "2r2rk1/pp2pp1p/3pbnpQ/q2N4/2P1P3/8/PP2BPPP/R4RK1 b - - 2 16",
   "line": [
    "Nd5"
   ],
   "spoken": "White can play a knight to d5 hitting e7...",
   "reanchor": true
  },
  {
   "ply": 32,
   "t": 3708,
   "fen": "2r2rk1/pp2pp1p/3p1npQ/q2b4/2P1P3/8/PP2BPPP/R4RK1 w - - 0 17",
   "line": [
    "Bxd5"
   ],
   "spoken": "...but after a bishop capture on d5, if White takes with the c-pawn the e-pawn drops.",
   "reanchor": true
  },
  {
   "ply": 33,
   "t": 3712,
   "fen": "2r2rk1/pp2pp1p/3p1npQ/q2P4/2P5/8/PP2BPPP/R4RK1 b - - 0 17",
   "line": [
    "exd5"
   ],
   "spoken": "And if White takes with the e-pawn, it's a pawn chain to attack.",
   "reanchor": true
  },
  {
   "ply": 34,
   "t": 3718.5,
   "fen": "2r2rk1/p3pp1p/3p1npQ/qp1P4/2P5/8/PP2BPPP/R4RK1 w - - 0 18",
   "line": [
    "b5"
   ],
   "spoken": "You already know b5 is one of Black's main queenside tools.",
   "reanchor": true
  },
  {
   "ply": 35,
   "t": 3722.5,
   "fen": "2r2rk1/p3pp1p/3p1npQ/qP1P4/8/8/PP2BPPP/R4RK1 b - - 0 18",
   "line": [
    "cxb5"
   ],
   "spoken": ""
  },
  {
   "ply": 36,
   "t": 3725.5,
   "fen": "5rk1/p3pp1p/3p1npQ/qP1P4/8/8/PPr1BPPP/R4RK1 w - - 1 19",
   "line": [
    "Rc2"
   ],
   "spoken": "After the capture you can take the pawn or infiltrate to c2 — Black is the only one having fun.",
   "reanchor": true
  },
  {
   "ply": 26,
   "t": 3733.5,
   "fen": "r4rk1/pp2ppbp/3pbnp1/q5B1/2P1P3/2N5/PP1QBPPP/R4RK1 w - - 12 14",
   "line": [],
   "spoken": ""
  },
  {
   "ply": 27,
   "t": 3738.5,
   "fen": "r4rk1/pp2ppbp/3pbnp1/q5B1/2P1PP2/2N5/PP1QB1PP/R4RK1 b - - 0 14",
   "line": [
    "f4"
   ],
   "spoken": "If White pushes f4, it creates no threat.",
   "reanchor": true
  },
  {
   "ply": 28,
   "t": 3741.5,
   "fen": "2r2rk1/pp2ppbp/3pbnp1/q5B1/2P1PP2/2N5/PP1QB1PP/R4RK1 w - - 1 15",
   "line": [
    "Rac8"
   ],
   "spoken": "So we continue with a rook to c8, and after b3...",
   "reanchor": true
  },
  {
   "ply": 29,
   "t": 3744.5,
   "fen": "2r2rk1/pp2ppbp/3pbnp1/q5B1/2P1PP2/1PN5/P2QB1PP/R4RK1 b - - 0 15",
   "line": [
    "b3"
   ],
   "spoken": "...you should already know Black's move.",
   "reanchor": true
  },
  {
   "ply": 30,
   "t": 3751.5,
   "fen": "2r2rk1/p3ppbp/3pbnp1/qp4B1/2P1PP2/1PN5/P2QB1PP/R4RK1 w - - 0 16",
   "line": [
    "b5"
   ],
   "spoken": "When b3 is played, always test the immediate b5 — here it works because the queen on d2 hangs, since f4 severed the bishop-queen connection.",
   "reanchor": true
  },
  {
   "ply": 26,
   "t": 3765.5,
   "fen": "r4rk1/pp2ppbp/3pbnp1/q5B1/2P1P3/2N5/PP1QBPPP/R4RK1 w - - 12 14",
   "line": [],
   "spoken": "There are so many of these lines, but that's enough.",
   "reanchor": true
  },
  {
   "ply": 13,
   "t": 3769.5,
   "fen": "r1bqkb1r/pp1ppp1p/5np1/8/2PQP3/2N5/PP3PPP/R1B1KB1R b KQkq - 0 7",
   "line": [],
   "spoken": "A good introduction to this line.",
   "reanchor": true
  },
  {
   "ply": 11,
   "t": 3771,
   "fen": "r1bqkb1r/pp1ppp1p/2n2np1/8/2PNP3/2N5/PP3PPP/R1BQKB1R b KQkq - 2 6",
   "line": [],
   "spoken": ""
  },
  {
   "ply": 13,
   "t": 3780,
   "fen": "r1bqkb1r/pp1ppp1p/5np1/8/2PQP3/2N5/PP3PPP/R1B1KB1R b KQkq - 0 7",
   "line": [
    "Nxd4",
    "Qxd4"
   ],
   "spoken": "A knight capture on c4 wasn't possible, because White takes on e4.",
   "reanchor": true
  },
  {
   "ply": 14,
   "t": 3781,
   "fen": "r1bqkb1r/pp2pp1p/3p1np1/8/2PQP3/2N5/PP3PPP/R1B1KB1R w KQkq - 0 8",
   "line": [
    "d6"
   ],
   "spoken": ""
  },
  {
   "ply": 16,
   "t": 3783.5,
   "fen": "r1bqk2r/pp2ppbp/3p1np1/8/2PQP3/2N5/PP2BPPP/R1B1K2R w KQkq - 2 9",
   "line": [
    "Be2",
    "Bg7"
   ],
   "spoken": "After castles, a bishop to e6, a queen to e2, a queen to a5, f4, a rook to c8, and b3, the knight capture on c4 is bad because White takes on e4 with two pieces for a rook. Black is fine but nothing special — its rooks are bad, no open files. Two-pieces-for-a-rook is an imbalance decided case by case, which is why higher-rated players seek imbalanced positions: they're harder for a lower-rated player to evaluate.",
   "reanchor": true
  },
  {
   "ply": 10,
   "t": 3854.5,
   "fen": "r1bqkb1r/pp1ppp1p/2n2np1/8/2PNP3/8/PP3PPP/RNBQKB1R w KQkq - 1 6",
   "line": [],
   "spoken": "Two pieces for a rook is generally good for the pieces, so you need good justification to take the rook's side.",
   "reanchor": true
  },
  {
   "ply": 11,
   "t": 3856.5,
   "fen": "r1bqkb1r/pp1ppp1p/2n2np1/8/2PNP3/5P2/PP4PP/RNBQKB1R b KQkq - 0 6",
   "line": [
    "f3"
   ],
   "spoken": "Now our opponent's f3 — there are interesting tactics here.",
   "reanchor": true
  },
  {
   "ply": 12,
   "t": 3872,
   "fen": "r1bqkb1r/pp1ppp1p/5np1/8/2PnP3/5P2/PP4PP/RNBQKB1R w KQkq - 0 7",
   "line": [
    "Nxd4"
   ],
   "spoken": "A knight capture on d4 is all right, but not the best.",
   "reanchor": true
  },
  {
   "ply": 11,
   "t": 3874,
   "fen": "r1bqkb1r/pp1ppp1p/2n2np1/8/2PNP3/5P2/PP4PP/RNBQKB1R b KQkq - 0 6",
   "line": [],
   "spoken": ""
  },
  {
   "ply": 12,
   "t": 3875,
   "fen": "r1bqk2r/pp1pppbp/2n2np1/8/2PNP3/5P2/PP4PP/RNBQKB1R w KQkq - 1 7",
   "line": [
    "Bg7"
   ],
   "spoken": "The engine's best is indeed a bishop to g7.",
   "reanchor": true
  },
  {
   "ply": 13,
   "t": 3878,
   "fen": "r1bqk2r/pp1pppbp/2n2np1/8/2PNP3/4BP2/PP4PP/RN1QKB1R b KQkq - 2 7",
   "line": [
    "Be3"
   ],
   "spoken": "White plays a bishop to e3, and here we rely on a trap.",
   "reanchor": true
  },
  {
   "ply": 4,
   "t": 3894.5,
   "fen": "r1bqkbnr/pp1ppppp/2n5/2p5/4P3/5N2/PPPP1PPP/RNBQKB1R w KQkq - 2 3",
   "line": [],
   "spoken": "To understand it you have to know the most famous Accelerated Dragon trap.",
   "reanchor": true
  },
  {
   "ply": 7,
   "t": 3895.5,
   "fen": "r1bqkbnr/pp1ppppp/2n5/8/3NP3/8/PPP2PPP/RNBQKB1R b KQkq - 0 4",
   "line": [
    "d4",
    "cxd4",
    "Nxd4"
   ],
   "spoken": ""
  },
  {
   "ply": 9,
   "t": 3897.5,
   "fen": "r1bqkbnr/pp1ppp1p/2n3p1/8/3NP3/2N5/PPP2PPP/R1BQKB1R b KQkq - 1 5",
   "line": [
    "g6",
    "Nc3"
   ],
   "spoken": "It occurs when White tries to play it like a regular Dragon.",
   "reanchor": true
  },
  {
   "ply": 11,
   "t": 3899,
   "fen": "r1bqk1nr/pp1pppbp/2n3p1/8/3NP3/2N1B3/PPP2PPP/R2QKB1R b KQkq - 3 6",
   "line": [
    "Bg7",
    "Be3"
   ],
   "spoken": ""
  },
  {
   "ply": 12,
   "t": 3902.5,
   "fen": "r1bqk2r/pp1pppbp/2n2np1/8/3NP3/2N1B3/PPP2PPP/R2QKB1R w KQkq - 4 7",
   "line": [
    "Nf6"
   ],
   "spoken": "White plays a bishop to c4, we castle, and White makes all his normal Dragon moves.",
   "reanchor": true
  },
  {
   "ply": 13,
   "t": 3904,
   "fen": "r1bqk2r/pp1pppbp/2n2np1/8/2BNP3/2N1B3/PPP2PPP/R2QK2R b KQkq - 5 7",
   "line": [
    "Bc4"
   ],
   "spoken": ""
  },
  {
   "ply": 15,
   "t": 3906.5,
   "fen": "r1bq1rk1/pp1pppbp/2n2np1/8/2BNP3/2N1BP2/PPP3PP/R2QK2R b KQ - 0 8",
   "line": [
    "O-O",
    "f3"
   ],
   "spoken": "What's the punishment — the famous trap Bobby Fischer fell into against Oscar Panno?",
   "reanchor": true
  },
  {
   "ply": 16,
   "t": 3923,
   "fen": "r1b2rk1/pp1pppbp/1qn2np1/8/2BNP3/2N1BP2/PPP3PP/R2QK2R w KQ - 1 9",
   "line": [
    "Qb6"
   ],
   "spoken": "It's not a knight capture on c4, which drops a piece — you set it up with the counterintuitive queen to b6, because the bishop on e3 is undefended.",
   "reanchor": true
  },
  {
   "ply": 17,
   "t": 3928,
   "fen": "r1b2rk1/pp1pppbp/1qN2np1/8/2B1P3/2N1BP2/PPP3PP/R2QK2R b KQ - 0 9",
   "line": [
    "Nxc6"
   ],
   "spoken": ""
  },
  {
   "ply": 18,
   "t": 3931,
   "fen": "r1b2rk1/pp1pppbp/2N2np1/8/2B1P3/2N1qP2/PPP3PP/R2QK2R w KQ - 0 10",
   "line": [
    "Qxe3+"
   ],
   "spoken": "So a queen capture on e3 with check would win.",
   "reanchor": true
  },
  {
   "ply": 16,
   "t": 3933,
   "fen": "r1b2rk1/pp1pppbp/1qn2np1/8/2BNP3/2N1BP2/PPP3PP/R2QK2R w KQ - 1 9",
   "line": [],
   "spoken": "The common response is a knight to f5...",
   "reanchor": true
  },
  {
   "ply": 17,
   "t": 3934,
   "fen": "r1b2rk1/pp1pppbp/1qn2np1/5N2/2B1P3/2N1BP2/PPP3PP/R2QK2R b KQ - 2 9",
   "line": [
    "Nf5"
   ],
   "spoken": "...but now we grab the pawn on b2 and Black wins.",
   "reanchor": true
  },
  {
   "ply": 18,
   "t": 3936.5,
   "fen": "r1b2rk1/pp1pppbp/2n2np1/5N2/2B1P3/2N1BP2/PqP3PP/R2QK2R w KQ - 0 10",
   "line": [
    "Qxb2"
   ],
   "spoken": "A knight to f5, a queen to b2 hitting the c3 knight — and we also win a bishop, so White loses pieces. If White defends the pawn with a bishop to b3, you play a knight capture on c4: three attackers, two defenders, and the e3 bishop drops. If a knight to f5, a knight capture on c3 hits the queen and evacuates the hanging knight. You have to build the foundations of opening knowledge — there's no way around it.",
   "reanchor": true
  }
 ]
}